# Tailscale SERVICE-NODE TLS: the bundled proxy joins your tailnet as its own
# virtual node (tsnet) named after your address's first label, and serves
# Cobblr at https://<name>.<tailnet>.ts.net with a real, auto-renewed cert.
# The BOX itself needs no Tailscale install; only the devices you browse from
# are on the tailnet.
#
# Requires in .env:
#   COBBLR_SITE_ADDRESS = cobblr.<your-tailnet>.ts.net
#     MUST be a name this node owns, tailnet included. Only the first label is
#     used to register, so a wrong tailnet still joins and still reports
#     Connected while no cert is ever issued, and the browser fails with
#     SSL_ERROR_INTERNAL_ERROR_ALERT. Read the tailnet from the admin console's
#     DNS page rather than copying the shape of an example.
#   TS_AUTHKEY          = tskey-auth-...           (OPTIONAL, see below)
#
# Joining the tailnet, two ways:
#   * No TS_AUTHKEY: the entrypoint runs the node interactively and the caddy
#     logs print a one-time approval link. Open it, sign in, approve. Easiest.
#   * TS_AUTHKEY set: a headless join with a reusable key from the admin console.
#
# Tailnet prerequisites: MagicDNS + HTTPS certificates enabled (admin console,
# DNS page). After the node first appears, disable its key expiry in the admin
# console or it deauthenticates in ~6 months (this applies to both paths). Node
# identity persists under /data (bind-mounted), so restarts keep the same node.
#
# COBBLR_TSNET_NAME is derived by the entrypoint from the address's first
# label (cobblr.tail1234.ts.net -> "cobblr"); set it only to override.

{$COBBLR_SITE_ADDRESS} {
	bind tailscale/{$COBBLR_TSNET_NAME}
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy web:8080
}
